REGENT OF BANTUL,

Considering : a. that every child and woman has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security, freedom from all forms of violence, discrimination and violations of the rights of women and children;
b. that acts of violence against children and women continue to increase, thus requiring comprehensive and maximum protection efforts, concrete actions, formal institutional support, regulations that can guarantee implementation by the Regional Government in increasing broad community participation;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within the Special Region of Jogjakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
